<title>FRANCE: Essilor rises on option deal.</title>
<headline>Essilor rises on option deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Essilor shares rose strongly on Tuesday, bucking a weaker overall market, after Oakley Inc of the United States announced it had agreed to an option to buy the non-prescription lens production unit of the French company's U.S. arm, Gentex Optics.</p>
<p>At 1415 GMT, Essilor shares were up 3.32 percent or 43 francs at 1,338 francs on volume of 14,660 shares traded while the CAC-40 index of leading shares was down 0.08 percent.</p>
<p>Brokerage Cheuvreux-de-Virieu remarked favourably on the transaction in its daily market comment, dealers said.</p>
<p>The option to purchase is not exercisable by Oakley until the expiry of a four-year licence to be granted to Oakley by Essilor and Gentex.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
